Review follow-ups on #383:
- FU2: wire verifyJournal into `forge serve` STARTUP (verifyJournalAtStartup),
  warning loudly on a broken chain but never blocking — the tamper-evident
  control now actually runs on every serve, not only in tests. Injectable warn
  sink; two tests assert warn-on-tamper and silence on intact/absent journal.
- security-model.md precision: (a) delete-detection now says a NON-TAIL deletion
  breaks the next prevHash and that tail truncation is only catchable with an
  externally anchored head hash (filed follow-up); (b) journal line tightened to
  "every token-valid mutation attempt" (403 returns before the append); (c) token
  wording softened to describe CLIENT behavior, noting readRequestToken's
  pre-existing ?token= query fallback can put a token in a request line/log.

Follow-ups (external head-hash anchor; journaling failed-auth probes) are filed
separately, not in this PR.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
